<div class="exercise"><div class="ex-q"><p>Why does a robot’s <code>odom</code> pose never jump, while its pose in <code>map</code> may?</p>
</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class="ex-s"><p>Odometry is continuous by construction (it only integrates small motions), which control loops need. Corrections from a localiser are applied to the <code>map → odom</code> transform, which may jump when a correction arrives, without disturbing the smooth <code>odom</code> pose.</p>
</div></details></div>
